# {{ .Project.Name }}

TypeScript React Router application. Package identity is fixed as tplaiter-web-app to preserve the exact producer-generated Bun lock across project names.

After a separately approved frozen installation with Bun1.4.2 and the declared runtime, these scripts are available:

```sh
bun install --frozen-lockfile --ignore-scripts
bun run dev
bun run build
bun run typecheck
bun run test
bun run lint
```

The template does not itself authorize acquisition or native execution. A missing bun.lock is an unfinished source candidate; never regenerate one from an ambient cache or perform an unfrozen fallback install.

VITE_API_BASE_URL is public browser configuration. The default /api/ API must implement GET/POST items, PUT/DELETE items/:id; item fields are exactly id, title and completed. List responses are unique item arrays; create/update return an item; deletion returns204. No server/database or credentials are generated. Transport uses explicit cancellation, bounded JSON, credentials omission and redirect refusal. Development backend CORS must explicitly permit the chosen public application origin.

Home, Items and not-found are real data-router routes. The route generator registers lazy pages; the page generator creates a standalone module only. Generated component/feature/API modules use the shared primitives and decoders. Skill and block catalogs are source artifacts with separately qualified selection; no formatter or installed action is inferred from them.
